---
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import SEO from '../components/SEO.astro';
import '../styles/global.css';
---

<html lang="en-GB">
  <head>
    <SEO
      title="Editorial Policy — British Home Interior"
      description="How British Home Interior researches, writes, and updates content — our sourcing standards, correction policy, and independence from brands."
      type="website"
      canonicalPath="/editorial-policy/"
    />
  </head>
  <body>
    <noscript><iframe src="https://www.googletagmanager.com/ns.html?id=GTM-KZHMLD9Q"
    height="0" width="0" style="display:none;visibility:hidden"></iframe></noscript>
    <Header />

    <main class="policy-page">
      <section class="policy-hero">
        <div class="policy-hero-inner">
          <span class="policy-eyebrow">How We Work</span>
          <h1 class="policy-heading">Editorial Policy</h1>
          <p class="policy-sub">How we research, write, and correct what we publish.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-body">
        <div class="policy-inner">

          <div class="policy-block">
            <h2>Who writes this</h2>
            <p>
              British Home Interior is written and maintained by Badreddine, based in the UK. This
              isn't a large editorial team — it's one person researching and testing real ideas for
              British homes, then writing up what actually works and what doesn't. See the
              <a href="/about/">About page</a> for the full story.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="policy-block">
            <h2>How we research and write</h2>
            <p>
              Every guide is built around the reality of British housing: period terraces, rented
              flats, and tenancy restrictions that most home styling content (much of it American)
              simply doesn't account for. Prices and retailers are checked against UK sources —
              Dunelm, IKEA UK, Next Home, John Lewis, Wayfair UK, B&Q, Homebase, Amazon UK — rather
              than converted from US content.
            </p>
            <p>
              We use AI-assisted tools to help with research, drafting, and editing efficiency. Every
              piece of advice, every price, and every product recommendation is reviewed by a human
              before publishing — nothing goes live unchecked.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="policy-block">
            <h2>Product recommendations</h2>
            <p>
              We recommend specific products because they're genuinely useful for British homes and
              rented flats, not because of a paid placement. If a post ever contains a sponsored
              product or affiliate link, it will be clearly disclosed at the top of that article. As of
              now, this site does not run affiliate links or sponsored content.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="policy-block">
            <h2>Corrections and updates</h2>
            <p>
              Prices, retailer stock, and product availability change. If you spot something outdated
              or incorrect, <a href="/contact/">let us know</a> — we update posts when we confirm an
              error, and note significant changes in the post's "last updated" date rather than
              silently editing published claims.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="policy-block">
            <h2>What we don't do</h2>
            <ul>
              <li>We don't publish staged, unrealistic "after" photos we haven't actually recreated in a real UK home.</li>
              <li>We don't inflate prices or omit cheaper alternatives to make a paid product look better.</li>
              <li>We don't accept payment in exchange for a positive review.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="policy-block">
            <p class="policy-contact-line">
              Questions about how a specific post was researched or written? <a href="/contact/">Contact us</a> — we're happy to explain.
            </p>
          </div>

        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>

<style>
.policy-page { background: var(--color-bg); }

.policy-hero {
  background: var(--color-heading);
  padding: 6rem 2rem 4rem;
}
.policy-hero-inner { max-width: 780px; margin: 0 auto; }
.policy-eyebrow {
  font-family: var(--font-body);
  font-size: 0.72rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: 0.18em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--color-gold);
  display: block;
  margin-bottom: 1rem;
}
.policy-heading {
  font-family: var(--font-display);
  font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5vw, 3.4rem);
  font-weight: 700;
  color: #fff;
  margin: 0 0 1rem;
  line-height: 1.1;
}
.policy-sub {
  font-family: var(--font-body);
  font-size: 1rem;
  color: rgba(255,255,255,0.72);
  margin: 0;
}

.policy-body { background: #fff; padding: 4.5rem 2rem 6rem; }
.policy-inner { max-width: 780px; margin: 0 auto; }
.policy-block { margin-bottom: 2.75rem; }
.policy-block:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
.policy-block h2 {
  font-family: var(--font-display);
  font-size: 1.5rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--color-heading);
  margin: 0 0 1rem;
}
.policy-block p {
  font-size: 0.95rem;
  line-height: 1.85;
  color: var(--color-text-muted);
  margin: 0 0 1.1rem;
}
.policy-block p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
.policy-block a { color: var(--color-gold); }
.policy-block ul {
  margin: 0;
  padding-left: 1.3rem;
  color: var(--color-text-muted);
}
.policy-block ul li {
  font-size: 0.95rem;
  line-height: 1.85;
  margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
}
.policy-contact-line {
  font-family: var(--font-display);
  font-style: italic;
  font-size: 1.05rem !important;
  color: var(--color-gold) !important;
}

@media (max-width: 640px) {
  .policy-hero { padding: 4rem 1.25rem 3rem; }
  .policy-body { padding: 3rem 1.25rem 4rem; }
}
</style>
